      "content": "thanks. that's exactly what i needed. the second point is pretty easy to dismantle, so that will work great for the rebuttal phase. \n\none thing though—when you were writing the first part, you used some pretty strong words like \"inherently more moral\" to describe the state of peace under deterrence. do you think that's a fair way to frame it, or is it just a specific way of looking at it? i want to make sure my student knows if they're stating a fact or just an interpretation.",
